To decompose the mission into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we will break down the mission description into goals and tasks using the specified structure. Here's how the decomposition can be structured:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                     | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Food to Inpatient Room | Ensure food is delivered to the inpatient room as per requests.      | -                  | Achieve   | -        |
| G2      | Determine Retrieval Method     | Decide how the food will be retrieved by the inpatient or others.    | FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2) | Query     | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Food                   | Deliver food to the room table or tray.                              | #                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G4      | Track Meal Retrieval           | Track which meal is retrieved and alert if incorrect.                | -                  | Achieve   | G1       |
| G5      | Retrieve Dirty Dishes          | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room.                                 | -                  | Achieve   | G1       |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                     | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location           | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------ | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Room               | Move robot to the designated inpatient room.                         | AND      | Inpatient Room     | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Place Food on Table            | Place the food on the room table if possible.                        | AND      | Inpatient Room     | 1                |
| AT3     | Indicate Meal for Retrieval    | Indicate which meal should be retrieved by the inpatient.            | AND      | Inpatient Room     | 1                |
| AT4     | Alert Incorrect Meal Retrieval | Alert if the wrong meal is retrieved by the inpatient.               | AND      | Inpatient Room     | 1                |
| AT5     | Open Room Door                 | Open the room door, possibly with cooperation.                       | OR       | Inpatient Room     | [1, n]           |
| AT6     | Retrieve Dishes                | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room.                                 | AND      | Inpatient Room     | [1, n]           |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3, G4, G5 [AND]**: All sub-goals must be fulfilled to achieve the main goal of delivering food.
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [FALLBACK]**: Determine if the inpatient can retrieve the food or if assistance is needed.
  - **G2.1**: Query if inpatient can retrieve food.
  - **G2.2**: Query if a companion or nurse is available.
- **G3 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**: Delivering food involves navigating to the room and placing the food.
- **G4 -> AT3, AT4 [AND]**: Tracking meal retrieval involves indicating the meal and alerting if incorrect.
- **G5 -> AT5, AT6 [AND]**: Retrieving dishes involves opening the door and retrieving the dishes.

This decomposition ensures that each goal and task is clearly defined and related, following the hierarchical structure required for a multi-robot system.
